    {
      "id": "s003",
      "title": "Passage 3",
      "text": "Saving a little less. Stopping new retirement contributions. And retiring altogether. Those require very different amounts of money. You might have enough invested to reduce contributions while continuing to work for another twenty years. That doesn\u2019t mean you can quit next Tuesday. Your paycheck still needs to cover your life. And your investments still need time. The idea that your existing investments could grow enough to fund a later retirement is often called Coast FIRE.",
