    {
      "id": "s011",
      "title": "Passage 11",
      "text": "You might discover that a modest reduction still supports your goal. Or that the trade-off costs more future freedom than you want to give up. Either answer is useful. If you do reduce contributions, consider keeping enough to capture your employer\u2019s full match, if offered, and check the plan\u2019s rules and vesting conditions. Then try a measured reduction rather than treating this as a permanent switch. Choose the amount. Decide where the extra take-home pay goes. Put a review date on the calendar.",
